        "**Continuous monitoring** is a standing program of near real-time collection and analysis of security telemetry, not an occasional scan. Its purpose is to shorten attacker dwell time and catch intrusions while they are still moving (for example during lateral movement). In NIST CSF it sits under the **Detect** function.",
        "**Network** telemetry: firewall logs, IDS/IPS (Snort, Suricata), NetFlow, DNS logs (Zeek), and cloud flow data such as AWS VPC Flow Logs or Azure Network Watcher. Best for C2 callbacks, DNS exfiltration, DGA domains, east-west traffic and unusual egress.",
