        "**Asymmetric** encryption uses a public/private key pair: solves key exchange but is too slow for bulk data. RSA (based on factoring; 2048-bit ≈ 112-bit symmetric strength), ECC (256-bit ≈ 3072-bit RSA; the modern TLS default) and Diffie-Hellman (key agreement).",
