        "**CPU**: sustained high CPU from an unexpected process points to cryptojacking (common on cloud instances and Kubernetes, where the victim pays the bill) or cracking tools. GuardDuty reports `CryptoCurrency:EC2/BitcoinTool.B`; in Process Explorer check path, parent and whether the name fits the image (svchost in AppData at 80% CPU is malware).",
