        "**BOLA/IDOR abuse**: an authenticated session walking `/api/users/10001`, `10002`, `10003`… with a mix of 200s and 403s is enumerating objects it should not see. Other quiet attacks: low-rate credential stuffing paced under rate limits, and **session hijacking** (one token used from two IPs at once, or a mid-session geo or device change).",
        "Other application indicators: accounts created in the app or database outside provisioning (persistence), unexpected output (stack traces, SQL errors, defacement, data where it should not be), POSTs to unexpected files in upload folders (web shell), and web or database servers starting outbound connections (reverse shell, tool download, SSRF).",
        "UEBA baselines each user and API client (normally 30 calls an hour, 3,000 today) and catches low-and-slow abuse that static thresholds miss. ATT&CK: T1190, T1059 (command execution through injection), T1078 when valid credentials are abused.",
