        "MISP tags (TLP, ATT&CK IDs, kill chain phases, sectors) travel with events, and **warning lists** flag known-good infrastructure such as public DNS resolvers to prevent false-positive blocks. Exports: STIX, OpenIOC, CSV, JSON and a REST API feeding SIEM and SOAR. Check distribution and tags before automating; some intel is for human analysis only.",
        "**OpenCTI** (open source, created by ANSSI with CERT-EU): a **STIX 2.1 knowledge graph** where the value is in relationships (actor uses malware, malware exploits vulnerability). Objects include threat actor, **intrusion set** (activity believed to be one operation but not yet attributed), campaign, attack pattern, malware, tool, indicator and observable.",
        "OpenCTI **observable** vs **indicator**: an observable is raw data you saw (IP, hash, domain); an indicator is an observable judged malicious, with reasoning, and is what you act on. ATT&CK integration compares an actor's techniques with your detection coverage, and connectors pull in MISP, OTX, VirusTotal, ATT&CK and CISA KEV.",
        "Searching the TIP during triage shows at once whether an indicator has been seen before, in which reports and incidents, and with what confidence.",
