        "**Pyramid of Pain** (David J. Bianco, 2013) ranks indicators by how much it hurts the attacker when you detect and deny them, bottom to top: **hash values** (trivial: change one byte), **IP addresses** (easy: new cloud host, proxy or dynamic DNS), **domain names** (simple: registration costs a little, and DGAs automate thousands), **network/host artifacts** (annoying: URI patterns, user-agent strings, C2 structure, registry keys, mutexes, service names), **tools** (challenging: malware and frameworks must be acquired or rebuilt), **TTPs** (tough: they must change how they operate).",
