        "**APT lifecycle**: weeks of reconnaissance (staff profiles, job postings that reveal the tech stack, conference talks) → targeted initial access (spear phishing, watering holes, supply chain, public-facing exploits) → several redundant persistence mechanisms (scheduled tasks, services, Run keys, rogue accounts, web shells) → lateral movement by living off the land (PsExec, WMI, PowerShell) with stolen credentials → slow, small, encrypted exfiltration (cloud storage, DNS tunneling, steganography) that stays under DLP thresholds.",
