        "**Insider threat**: anyone who has or had authorized access (employees, former employees, contractors, vendors, partners). **Intentional** insiders act from financial gain, disgruntlement, ideology or coercion; respond with HR and legal involvement and careful evidence preservation. **Unintentional** insiders click phishing links, misconfigure cloud storage or email PII to the wrong person; respond with remediation, training and process fixes.",
