        "**STIX** (Structured Threat Information Expression), currently version 2.1, is a JSON format for threat intelligence. Each object has a `type`, such as `indicator`, `malware`, `threat-actor`, `attack-pattern`, `campaign`, `vulnerability` or `observed-data`, plus `relationship` objects linking them (e.g. malware uses an attack pattern). Objects are grouped in bundles.",
