        "A **security operations center (SOC)** is the centralized team and technology that monitors, detects, analyzes and responds to threats around the clock. Attackers favor off-hours (2 AM on a Sunday); without a SOC, breaches tend to be discovered weeks later by a customer or a reporter.",
        "**Internal SOC**: built and staffed in-house; suits large enterprises and government that need tight control of data. **Managed SOC (MSSP)**: a managed security service provider monitors remotely; suits smaller organizations that want 24/7 coverage without the overhead. **Hybrid**: a mix, e.g. Tier 1 and 2 in-house with after-hours monitoring outsourced; common in mid-sized organizations.",
        "Four core functions: **continuous monitoring** (the SIEM collects, correlates and alerts on firewall, endpoint, cloud and application logs), **alert triage and investigation** (true or false positive, scope, pivot from the SIEM alert into EDR telemetry for the same time window), **incident response coordination** (containment, eradication, recovery, stakeholder communication) and **metrics and reporting**.",
