        "Intrusions follow a structure: scope the target, build or buy tooling, deliver it, gain a foothold, then pursue the goal (theft, disruption or quiet persistence). Frameworks give analysts a map and a shared vocabulary to turn scattered alerts into a story.",
        "**Cyber Kill Chain** (Lockheed Martin, 2011, adapted from military targeting): a linear seven-phase model. Answers: **where is the attacker in the sequence?** Simple, easy to explain to non-technical people and maps cleanly to defensive controls. Weakness: real attacks are not linear.",
        "**Diamond Model** (Caltagirone, Pendergast and Betz, 2013): a relational model of adversary, capability, infrastructure and victim. Answers: **who, with what, through what, against whom, and how do events connect?** Strong for attribution and correlation. Weakness: no built-in sequence or timeline.",
