        "Right message, right person, right channel, right time. To a CISO: 'CVE-2024-21412, CVSS 9.8, SmartScreen bypass on unpatched Windows 11.' To a CFO: 'An actively exploited flaw lets financially motivated attackers bypass endpoint defenses and reach financial systems.'",
        "**Technical teams** (sysadmins, patch teams, engineers): precision (CVE, CVSS, versions, exact fix, testing and rollback guidance, deadline) delivered as the ticket with the linked scanner finding and NVD reference. No narrative.",
        "**IT management**: scope, timeline, resources and dependencies, through a tracking view of open findings against SLA, action plans and escalations.",
        "**Executives** (CISO, CIO, board): business risk, trend, financial and operational impact, compliance, cost to fix and **risk acceptance** decisions, through scorecards, dashboards and a short narrative. Lead acceptance requests with business impact, e.g. 'the end-of-life payment system could expose cardholder data; it is isolated and monitored; we need formal acceptance.'",
        "**Compliance and audit**: evidence that the program runs: documented scanning, tracked remediation, escalations within timeframes and formally approved exceptions, with timestamps, scan configuration records, remediation audit trails and sign-offs.",
        "Cadence: weekly for operations, monthly for IT management, monthly or quarterly scorecards for executives, audit-cycle reports for compliance. Plus **event-driven urgent protocols** defined in advance: a new KEV entry hitting 40 systems means a call to the CISO, same-day owner emails with a 24-hour expectation and an emergency change ticket.",
        "Match technical literacy: too technical and non-technical readers disengage; too simple and practitioners lose what they need. Build relationships with system owners, because other teams do the fixing.",
