        "The attacker may be inside email, chat or even the IR lead's laptop. Posting 'we isolate the hosts at 14:00' in a compromised chat lets them cover tracks, switch to backup persistence or speed up exfiltration. In the SolarWinds intrusion (2020) attackers sat in victim environments for months, so in-environment IR communications were exposed.",
        "**OPSEC**: keeping incident information from unauthorized parties, including the attacker, while the team still coordinates.",
        "**Out-of-band channels** set up in advance (personal phones, Signal, a separate email domain, an isolated IR cloud tenant with no trust to corporate) and tested before tabletops, plus a printed contact sheet in the SOC.",
