        "The **after-action report (AAR)** or post-incident report is the full technical and operational record after containment and remediation, for the security team, management, auditors, regulators and legal. The executive summary is the short brief; the AAR is the complete record behind it.",
        "Six AAR sections: **incident summary** (type, detection, declaration, outcome); **incident timeline** (first indicator, alert, investigation start, declaration, each containment and remediation action, closure, built from SIEM, EDR, IR platform, communication logs and forensics, not memory; it also proves notification compliance); **technical analysis**; **impact assessment**; **response evaluation**; **recommendations**.",
        "**Technical analysis**: attack vector, initial access, lateral movement path, persistence, tools and TTPs mapped to ATT&CK (e.g. LSASS dumping `T1003.001`, scheduled task `T1053.005`), with an ATT&CK Navigator layer attached as a detection-engineering roadmap.",
