        "**Lessons learned review**: a structured debrief with all participants on what went well, what did not and what to change. Hold it as soon as practical (NIST), typically **within one to two weeks of closure**, with the IR team, affected business unit, IT operations, legal, communications/PR if involved and any external retainer.",
        "Agenda: timeline review (shared understanding, not blame); what worked (reinforce it); what did not (detection delays, communication breakdowns, slow containment, tool failures, skill gaps); specific recommendations with owner, timeline and cost. The output is a formal document added to the AAR.",
