        "SOCs run 8- or 12-hour shifts or follow the sun across time zones, and incidents ignore shift boundaries. Poor handovers lose context: re-imaging a host already imaged and under legal hold, duplicated investigations, or breaking a covert monitoring operation.",
        "A **handover** is a formal transfer of situational awareness, task ownership and decision authority, written first and verbal second. A verbal-only handover is a single point of failure.",
